# Shell / sandbox

When running any of these, always use Shell with `required_permissions: ["all"]`
(do not rely on the default sandbox):

- `./scripts/dev-start.sh`
- `./scripts/dev-stop.sh`
- `npm run test:e2e` / `npx playwright …`
- `npx playwright install …`

Reason:

- `dev-*.sh`: process signals (kill) and/or writes under `/Volumes`
- Playwright: browsers install/run against `~/Library/Caches/ms-playwright`
  (unset `PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH` if a sandbox injected it).
  A sandboxed shell cannot create the lock/cache dirs there → `EPERM`.

`npm run format`, `npm run lint`, `npm run type-check`, `npm run build`, and
`npm run test:unit` may stay sandboxed.
